  "ud4.8:2.1": "",
  "ud4.8:2.2": "Ānandajoti has “venture”, Ṭhānissaro has “dare”, but a similar phrase at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd8/en/sujato#12.1.5'>Kd 8:12.1.5</a> clearly has the weaker sense of “able”, per Ireland and commentary (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>ussahasīti sakkosi</i>). ",
  "ud4.8:2.3": "",
  "ud4.8:2.4": "Accepting the variant <i lang='pi' translate='no'>kiṁ mayā sakkā</i>, which is found in all similar passages. Reading, as Ṭhānissaro and Ānandajoti do, “what can I <em>not</em> do” is pleasingly dramatic, but not very idiomatic for Pali. Far more likely a simple reinforcement is meant. Commentary ignores this phrase, implying it thought there was nothing unusual. ",
  "ud4.8:2.5": "",
